/**
 * @mainpage pGRAMSFC (pGRAMS Flight Computer)
 *
 * Software for pGRAMS flight computer
 *
 * ## Author
 *
 * - Shota Arai
 *
 * ## Aims
 *
 * This repository is intended for the following usage:
 *
 * - Collect data from housekeeping (HK) sensors
 * - Create packets and send them to the ground
 * - Send commands from the ground
 * - Interpret the received packets to push to MySQL database for Grafana displaying
 *
 * ## Topics
 *
 * The classes are grouped into four categories. Each category is split into the core classes,
 * which are the library components, and the modules, which are the ANL Next modules assembled
 * by the operation scripts.
 *
 * - @ref device "Device" : hardware I/O and interface classes
 *   (@ref device_core "Core" / @ref device_module "Module")
 * - @ref daqcom "DAQ Communication" : communication with the DAQ computers
 *   (@ref daqcom_core "Core" / @ref daqcom_module "Module")
 * - @ref telecom "Telecom" : telemetry and command handling including MQTT
 *   (@ref telecom_core "Core" / @ref telecom_module "Module")
 * - @ref ground "Ground" : processing on the ground
 *   (@ref ground_core "Core" / @ref ground_module "Module")
 *
 * ## Structure
 *
 * - [onboard](https://github.com/STA205233/pGramsFC/tree/master/onboard) : Onboard software and ground receiver
 * - [command_sender](https://github.com/STA205233/pGramsFC/tree/master/command_sender) : Command sender software
 * - [operation](https://github.com/STA205233/pGramsFC/tree/master/operation) : Ruby scripts to execute the software
 * - [examples](https://github.com/STA205233/pGramsFC/tree/master/examples) : Example code for unit tests
 * - [service](https://github.com/STA205233/pGramsFC/tree/master/service) : Scripts to create deamon for onboard/ground software
 * - [settings](https://github.com/STA205233/pGramsFC/tree/master/settings) : Example of setting files
 * - [tools](https://github.com/STA205233/pGramsFC/tree/master/tools) : Useful tools and scripts for basic tests
 *
 * ## Environment
 *
 * - MacOS Tahoe
 * - Ubuntu 20.04
 *
 * ## Installation
 *
 * Please look at [this page](../docs/Installation.md).
 */
